# Real-time Updates - Simple Polling

## No WebSockets

This project uses **simple polling** for real-time updates. No WebSocket infrastructure.

## Polling Service

### Simple Polling Implementation
```javascript
// ✅ Simple polling service
class PollingService {
  constructor() {
    this.pollInterval = 30000; // 30 seconds
    this.isPolling = false;
  }

  startPolling() {
    if (this.isPolling) return;
    this.isPolling = true;
    // Polling handled by React Query refetchInterval
  }
}
```

### React Query Polling
```javascript
// ✅ Automatic polling with React Query
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['participants'],
  queryFn: fetchParticipants,
  refetchInterval: 30000, // 30 seconds
  staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000 // 5 minutes
});
```

## Data Updates

### Server-side Changes
```javascript
// ✅ Simple API responses
app.get('/api/participants', async (req, res) => {
  const participants = await executeQuery('SELECT * FROM participants');
  res.json({ success: true, data: participants });
});
```

### Client-side Updates
```javascript
// ✅ Automatic refetching
const queryClient = useQueryClient();

// Manual refetch
const refetch = () => {
  queryClient.invalidateQueries(['participants']);
};

// Automatic refetch every 30 seconds
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['participants'],
  queryFn: fetchParticipants,
  refetchInterval: 30000
});
```

## Benefits

- **Simple** - No complex WebSocket management
- **Reliable** - HTTP requests are more stable
- **Debuggable** - Easy to trace and debug
- **Scalable** - Works with load balancers
- **Maintainable** - Simple to understand and modify

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ WebSocket Infrastructure
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use WebSockets
const socket = io('ws://localhost:3000');
socket.on('participants:updated', handleUpdate);
socket.emit('participants:subscribe');
```

### ❌ Complex Real-time State
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use WebSocket state
const [socketConnected, setSocketConnected] = useState(false);
const [realTimeData, setRealTimeData] = useState([]);
```

### ❌ Event-driven Updates
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use complex event systems
const eventBus = new EventBus();
eventBus.on('data:updated', handleUpdate);
eventBus.emit('data:refresh');
```

## Polling Configuration

### Environment-based Polling
```javascript
// ✅ Configurable polling intervals
const POLLING_INTERVALS = {
  participants: 30000,  // 30 seconds
  rounds: 60000,        // 1 minute
  news: 120000,         // 2 minutes
  cityTips: 300000      // 5 minutes
};
```

### Conditional Polling
```javascript
// ✅ Poll only when needed
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['participants'],
  queryFn: fetchParticipants,
  refetchInterval: isActive ? 30000 : false,
  enabled: isActive
});
```

## Performance Considerations

- **30-second intervals** - Balance between real-time and performance
- **Stale time** - 5 minutes to avoid unnecessary requests
- **Background refetch** - Only when tab is active
- **Error handling** - Graceful degradation on network issues